Oliver Ickler. 4.1 additions (C) 2026 Akustikrausch (Andreas Wendorf). The
original parts stay with their authors; no claim is made on them.

Tom Beyer opened the ProTracker 4 source on Aminet
(mus/edit/PT4_Beta2_src.lha) under this condition:

  "Using this source code is allowed as long as the names of *all*
  developers are visible in the about requester of the executable."

ProTracker 4.1 keeps that condition: whoever builds on this source keeps
the names of all developers visible in the about box of the program.
ProTracker 3.15 was released by CryptoBurners as public domain.

